Fu-Kane-Mele on the diamond lattice, PRL 98, 106803 (2007): four bands, two
occupied, one of the four nearest-neighbour bonds detuned along [111].

1. the undistorted crystal
   realized group   : #227.129 Fd-3m1', s orbitals at Wyckoff 8a, 4 bands
   E at GM          : -4.000000, -4.000000, +4.000000, +4.000000   gap 8.000000
   E at L           : -2.000000, -2.000000, +2.000000, +2.000000   gap 4.000000
   E at W           : -1.000000, -1.000000, +1.000000, +1.000000   gap 2.000000
   E at X           : the four bands meet                          gap 0.000000
   all 4 bands      : -GM6 + -GM9 + -L8 + -L9 + -W5W6 + -W7 + -X5
   atomic limit     : 1 x -E1↑G(4)@8a(-43m1',-43m)
   valence content  : not defined at X, where all four bands meet
   the undistorted crystal is a semimetal

2. delta_t = +0.4 on the [111] bond
   realized group   : #166.98 R-3m1', orbitals at Wyckoff 6c: the detuned bond lowers
                      Fd-3m1' to R-3m1', with no atom moved
   E at GM          : -4.400000, -4.400000, +4.400000, +4.400000   gap 8.800000
   E at T           : -1.600000, -1.600000, +1.600000, +1.600000   gap 3.200000
   E at F           : -0.400000, -0.400000, +0.400000, +0.400000   gap 0.800000
   E at L           : -2.400000, -2.400000, +2.400000, +2.400000   gap 4.800000
   valence content  : -F5F6 + -GM9 + -L5L6 + -T8
   atomic limits    : none

3. delta_t = -0.4 on the same bond
   realized group   : #166.98 R-3m1', orbitals at Wyckoff 6c
   gaps GM/T/F/L    : 7.200000 / 4.800000 / 0.800000 / 3.200000
   valence content  : -F3F4 + -GM9 + -L5L6 + -T8
   atomic limits    : none

4. three bonds cut: decoupled dimers along [111]
   realized group   : #166.98 R-3m1', orbitals at Wyckoff 6c
   gaps GM/T/F/L    : 2.000000 / 2.000000 / 2.000000 / 2.000000
   valence content  : -F5F6 + -GM9 + -L5L6 + -T9
   atomic limit     : 1 x -E1u↑G(2)@3a(-3m1',-3m)
   the valence bands are the antibonding pair of each dimer's two s orbitals,
   centred at 3a on the [111] axis

5. the content at the eight time-reversal-invariant momenta (TRIM)
   k-orbits         : GM (1), T (1), F (3), L (3), covering the cell's 8 TRIM
   strong vs dimers : the content changes at T, 1 of the 8 TRIM
   weak vs dimers   : the content changes at F and T, 4 of the 8 TRIM
   #166.98 has inversion, so nu_0 is the parity product over these eight points

6. the symmetry-indicator class in {BS}/{AI}
   indicator group  : Z2 x Z4
   phase              class    order    z4   z2w,1/2/3   nu_0 = z4 mod 2
   strong             (0, 1)   4        3    1 1 1       1
   weak               (1, 0)   2        0    1 1 1       0
   dimers             (0, 0)   1        0    0 0 0       0
   Z2 indices       : strong (1;111), weak (0;111), dimers (0;000)

7. the bands along GM-T-F-L-GM, one panel per phase

